00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:01.189 align:start position:0%
 
hi  my name is ryan and i'd like to show you  around the google cloud console where  you can manage your google cloud  resources directly from the web  in the next few minutes we'll explore  several key areas of the console that  can help you as you begin your journey  with google cloud  ready let's get started  [Music]  google cloud resources are the  fundamental components that make up  google cloud services  these may include compute engine virtual  machines cloud storage buckets cloud sql  database instances and more  resources are organized hierarchically  using projects and folders  projects are how you group resources  together and are the first level of the  hierarchy all resources must belong to  exactly one project so a given compute  engine virtual machine or a cloud  storage bucket would belong to one  project  optionally projects can belong to  organizations which provide centralized  visibility and control across all  projects in a given org an organization  helps administrators for your company or  group manage billing or security across  many projects you can further organize  your company's departments or teams into  folders folders can contain projects and  also subfolders for further structure  and nesting  when you open console.cloud.google.com  here's the landing page dashboard  at the top you can see which google  cloud project you're currently viewing  you can click the project name to switch  to a different project  if you do so you'll see the resources  for your other project  you can also create a new project right  here  another key area of the console is the  left navigation menu located in the top  left corner  this menu helps you access your google  cloud services  for example if you navigate to the cloud  storage section you can create new cloud  storage buckets upload objects and  download objects you can also pin your  favorite products to the top for easy  access  i'll pin storage to make sure i can  quickly get to my buckets next time  next up we have the search bar which  allows you to quickly search for google  cloud products resources and  documentation  for example you could search for the  name of one of your other projects if  you want to switch to it  if you search for cloud run you'll see  links to the cloud run section of the  console  documentation and tutorials related to  cloud run and a list of cloud run  related apis that you might want to  manage  the home dashboard provides a high level  overview of your google cloud project  giving you information about key metrics  billing and getting started guides  the dashboard is customizable allowing  you to show hide and reorder the  different cards how you want  there's also the activity stream which  shows you information about all the  activities happening across your google  cloud resources in one place  for example you can see which projects  have been updated  what your teammates are doing or audit  access to your google cloud resources  next is the apis and services section  where you can do things like enable or  disable apis  view api usage information and manage  credentials  if you click enable apis and services at  the top you'll be brought to the api  library  this is where you can view information  about the hundreds of different google  cloud apis across areas like maps  machine learning google workspace and  more  if you click on cloud vision api you'll  be brought to the cloud vision api page  where you can click enable to enable the  api this allows you to use the vision  api in your applications  if you ever get stuck the support  section is also accessible right from  the navigation menu  you can get help via chat over the phone  or from other community members  there are several different support  offerings that you can compare and  contrast to see what makes the most  sense for you  another key part of the console is cloud  identity and access management or cloud  iam  here you can manage and create  permissions for your google cloud  resources  as your team grows you can grant access  to teammates in cloudiam  you can add users groups or service  accounts and assign them any number of  roles to grant them the permission they  need  for example you can add your friend  james as an editor for your google cloud  project  next up we have cloud shell which  provides you with command line access to  your cloud resources directly from your  web browser  powered by a small virtual machine with  persistent disk space it comes  pre-installed with helpful tools like  the google cloud sdk docker git and  various programming languages  this makes it easy to get started and  explore google cloud without having to  download additional software to your  local device  there's also cloud shell editor which  makes it easy for you to write code  directly from your web browser and  deploy it to the cloud  the billing section of the console is  where you can manage billing accounts  and link your projects to them  a cloud billing account defines who pays  for a given set of google cloud  resources  to use google cloud services you must  have a valid billing account linked to  your google cloud projects  the billing account can be linked to  payment methods like the free trial a  credit card or a bank account  there are also interactive quick start  experiences available in the console  these tutorials which you can find on  the home dashboard in the getting  started section  guide you through how to accomplish  essential tasks with different cloud  products  for example this tutorial guides you  through how to create a cloud storage  bucket upload a file to the bucket and  delete the bucket  and you can do this all in under five  minutes  beyond the web portal the google cloud  console is also available on android and  ios mobile apps  you can use these to monitor and manage  your google cloud applications on the go  so there you have it an overview of what  the google cloud console is and how you  can get started  make sure to check out the other  episodes of google cloud essentials  where we cover the google cloud sdk the  free trial key use cases and more  i can't wait to see what you built with  google cloud  [Music]  [Music]

